<title>CANADA: Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suncor Inc said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$12.00/cubic metre or C$1.91/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$218.00/cubic metre, or C$34.66/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$211.00/cubic metre, or C$33.55/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$185.00/cubic metre, or C$29.41/barrel</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
